-- Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two, six motorcycles (printed 200-206): Alley Cat, Black Talon, Electric CityCycle, Road Hog, Streetwolf, Wild Boar
-- 6 vehicle rows, with 29 locations and 1 weapon entries.
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration - it adds
-- rows, not schema.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/~323-northern-gun-2-motorcycles.sql
--
-- Written by scripts/vessel-sql.mjs from 1 worker file(s). Every value
-- is printable ASCII, every row cites its book, and a Main Body location
-- agrees with its vehicle's mdc_main_body.

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO vehicles (slug, name, system, vehicle_class, crew, passengers, speed_ground, speed_air, speed_water, dimensions, weight_tons, mdc_main_body, is_mega_damage, ar, cost, cost_note, description, source_book) VALUES
  ('ng-cm14-alley-cat-motorcycle', 'NG-CM14 Alley Cat Motorcycle', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'One pilot.', NULL, 'Maximum 100 mph (160 km); half that on grass, gravel and rough ground. Woodland and thick brush are likely impassable without a well-worn path, and even then under 10 mph (16 km).', NULL, NULL, 'Height 4 ft (1.2 m); width 3 ft (0.9 m); length 6 ft (1.8 m)', '240 lbs (108 kg)', 60, 1, NULL, 24000, '24,000 credits gasoline, 37,500 with the improved electric battery; offered in those two power systems only. A weapon is extra.', 'Model NG-CM14 (Class: All-Terrain Motorcycle). Designed by a team under Arnoldo Lefebre, Timothy Letts and C.M. Thomas for the rough dirt tracks and alleys of small towns, the ''Burbs and wilderness settlements, and for the rocky country of the American Southwest and northern Mexico, though it is happiest on paved city streets. Like most NG machines it shrugs off spills and hard use. Two headlights flank a bigger central lamp for unlit roads and alleys, and three hard-shell lockers (one per side, one behind the seat) draw City Rats, nomads, couriers, merchants, Black Marketeers and crooks who need somewhere to hide weapons, contraband or loot. Penalties: none on pavement, smooth surfaces or dirt roads; -5% piloting on short grass and stony desert, -10% on gravel and snow over 3 inches (7.6 cm), -25% on broken roads and tall grass; forest and wild country are likely impassable. Sand clogs the air intake and stalls the engine in 1D6 melee rounds. Range: 400 miles (640 km) on gasoline; 600 miles (960 km) per electric charge, recharging fully in under an hour. Cargo: a small built-in rear container about the size of one small suitcase, with room to lash a saddlebag, backpack or a bag or two to it. Weapons: none as standard; one light weapon from the hovercycle options may be bought, and about three buyers in four do without.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.200-201'),
  ('ng-mbt-300-black-talon-motorcycle', 'MBT-300 Black Talon Motorcycle', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'One pilot.', 'One.', 'Maximum 220 mph (352 km); 180 mph (288 km) over stony desert and dirt roads; 72 mph (115 km) or less on grassland and broken ground. Woodland and thick brush are likely impassable without a well-worn path, and even then under 8 mph (13 km).', NULL, NULL, 'Height 3.5 ft (1.1 m); width 3 ft (0.9 m); length 7 ft (2.1 m)', '420 lbs (189 kg)', 125, 1, NULL, 340000, '340,000 credits electric with a multi-battery system, 720,000 Solid Oxide, 945,000 nuclear with a 12 year life; the lowest is stored. No gasoline model is sold.', 'Model MBT-300 (Class: All-Terrain Combat Motorcycle). One of NG''s newest bikes, out in summer 108 P.A. from J.M. Volinsky, L.T. Stanley and Wilson Michaels (lead designers): a sleek, streamlined machine built for top speed, range and agility, and an immediate favourite of Juicers, Headhunters, Crazies, Highwaymen, Gladiators, robot pilots, Quick-Flex Aliens and anyone who loves going fast. Sold as all-terrain, it is at its best on pavement, dirt roads, alleys and the stony Southwestern and northern Mexican deserts; gravel and short grass (under a foot/0.3 m) slow it and cost skill. Penalties: none on pavement, dirt roads or stony desert; -10% piloting on gravel and grass, -15% on broken roads, tall grass and snow over 3 inches (7.6 cm); forest, thick brush and dense growth are likely impassable. Sand clogs the air intake and stalls the engine in 1D6 melee rounds. Range: 2,000 miles (3,200 km) per electric charge, two hours to recharge fully; unlimited on Solid Oxide or nuclear. The range line also gives 400 miles (640 km) on gasoline, though the cost line says no gasoline model exists. Cargo: saddlebags with little room; a rifle can be strapped to the side. Its headlight sits concealed beneath the nose weapon.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.201'),
  ('ng-em3-electric-citycycle', 'NG-EM3 Electric CityCycle', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'One pilot.', 'One.', 'Maximum 65 mph (104 km). Made for city streets and dirt roads; woodland and thick brush are impassable without a well-worn path, and even then rough going under 8 mph (13 km).', NULL, NULL, 'Height 3 ft (0.9 m); width 2 ft (0.6 m); length 5 ft (1.5 m)', '110 lbs (50 kg)', 60, 1, NULL, 19500, '19,500 credits; electric battery only, recharging fully in under 15 minutes.', 'Model NG-EM3 (Class: Electric Motorcycle). Most of Rifts Earth is wild to some degree, and people crowd into cities and city-states for safety and shared resources; a team under Donovan Pankratz, Albert Rosado and Doug Roy built this cheap electric bike for them, first shown in autumn 105 P.A. Internal gyroscopes hold it upright on its own, and it answers the rider''s intent, so it is easy to ride: +16% to the Motorcycle skill, and an untrained rider manages a base of 46%. Standing unaided, it parks anywhere and packs densely into depots and transports. It is no all-terrain machine, and its small battery ties it to charging stations, but it is cheap, dependable and suited to town; it has spread through Lazlo, Ishpeming, the Manistique Imperium, the ''Burbs and even big Coalition and Free Quebec cities, bought by private riders and by rental businesses. Special features: the gyro makes it hard to tip over even on purpose, and proximity sensors slow or halt it near traffic or obstacles, so it can seem to steer itself and needs no Piloting skill. Penalties: none on pavement or smooth ground; -10% piloting on dirt roads and stony desert, -20% on gravel and snow over 2 inches (5 cm), -40% on broken roads and tall grass; forest and wild country are likely impassable. Sand clogs the motors and stops the bike in 1D6 melee rounds. Range: 350 miles (560 km), electric only. Cargo: two zip-up saddlebags of about 10 lbs (4.5 kg) each. Weapons: none.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.202'),
  ('ng-road-hog-motorcycle', 'Road Hog Motorcycle', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'One pilot.', 'One is possible, but uncomfortable on long trips.', 'Maximum 160 mph (256 km) on pavement, dirt, short grass, gravel roads and stony desert; no more than 100 mph (160 km) on sand, tall grass and broken ground. Woodland and thick brush are likely impassable without a well-worn path, and even then under 15 mph (24 km). Thruster-assisted jumps of 15 ft (4.6 m) up and 50 ft (15.2 m) across with a good run, half again as far at 90 mph (144 km) or more.', NULL, NULL, 'Height 4 ft (1.2 m); width 2.6 ft (0.79 m); length 8 ft (2.4 m)', '850 lbs (382.5 kg)', 115, 1, NULL, 40000, '40,000 credits gasoline, 65,000 electric (with a folding solar charging station), 350,000 Solid Oxide, 875,000 nuclear; the lowest is stored. Weapons are extra.', 'All-Terrain Motorcycle; the entry prints no model number. From B. Whitcomb, B. Barton and L. Buck (team leaders): two huge, deeply ridged tires, each two feet (0.6 m) wide and built of light M.D.C. material, carry it over most rough country, and NG''s patented turbo thrusters, small nozzles, boost it into the air for jumps, with a heavy-duty suspension to cushion the landing. Jumps: built for rough ground and thruster leaps, it clears 15 ft (4.6 m) high and 50 ft (15.2 m) across with momentum, 50% more once the bike tops 90 mph (144 km), and landing even a long jump is only -8% to the piloting roll. It handles sand and dunes; the speed line prints that it crosses sand ''with fear of'' clogging, which the penalties line contradicts. Penalties: none on pavement, dirt roads and stony desert; -5% piloting on gravel and short grass, -10% on broken roads, sand, tall grass, and mud or snow up to a foot (0.3 m) deep; -30% in brush and snow over a foot deep; deeper mud, forest and dense growth are likely impassable. Range: 500 miles (800 km) on gasoline, 1,450 miles (2,320 km) per electric charge, unlimited on nuclear (rare) or Solid Oxide. Power: the electric model plugs into many sources and its solar station recharges it in six hours. Cargo: saddlebags only, about 10 lbs (4.5 kg) each. Weapons: optional, from the hovercycle range. The introduction allows 1-3 light weapons, a nose gun costing 3% of speed and jump distance and each other weapon 10%; the weapon line allows up to two added systems at 5% of top speed each.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.203-204'),
  ('ng-cm12-streetwolf-motorcycle', 'NG-CM12 Streetwolf Motorcycle', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'One pilot.', NULL, 'Maximum 240 mph (384 km); half that on dirt roads and stony desert, a third on grass, gravel and rough ground. Built for pavement and other hard, smooth surfaces; woodland and thick brush are likely impassable without a well-worn path, and even then under 10 mph (16 km).', NULL, NULL, 'Height 3 ft (0.9 m); width 2.6 ft (0.79 m); length 7 ft (2.1 m)', '240 lbs (108 kg)', 80, 1, NULL, 34000, '34,000 credits gasoline, 45,300 with the improved electric battery, 365,000 Solid Oxide, 900,000 nuclear (rare).', 'Model NG-CM12 (Class: Motorcycle). A low, fast sport bike from a team under G.G. Shore, Joseph Olewnicki and Kimihiro Hamaura, released in 107 P.A. and a hit at once with speed lovers. The rider crouches forward with feet set back, almost lying flat, which makes him hard to hit. Quick, nimble and well balanced, its slim low frame threads alleys, gaps between stalled cars and any tight space, which wins over City Rats, Black Marketeers, Highwaymen, couriers and racers; on city streets nothing beats it. Bonuses: on pavement, dirt roads and other smooth ground only, +5% piloting, including evasive and trick riding, and +1 to dodge. Penalties: short grass -5% piloting, gravel -15%, broken roads and mud or snow over 2 inches (5 cm) -20%, tall grass and deep snow or mud up to 6 inches (15 cm) -30%; forest and wild country are likely impassable. Sand clogs the air intake and stalls the engine in 1D4 melee rounds. Range: 400 miles (640 km) on gasoline; 1,800 miles (2,880 km) per electric charge, two hours to recharge fully; unlimited on Solid Oxide or nuclear. Cargo: none, though the location list prints a small rear storage compartment. Weapons: none, and none can be fitted without cost: even a nose gun upsets its balance, cutting speed 10% and cancelling the piloting bonus.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.204'),
  ('ng-wm330-wild-boar-motorcycle', 'NG-WM330 Wild Boar Motorcycle', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'One cyborg or other large rider.', 'One is possible with human-sized riders, but uncomfortable on long trips.', 'Maximum 130 mph (208 km) on pavement, dirt roads and stony desert; on grassland, sandy desert, broken roads and rough ground, 80 mph (128 km) at best, depending on conditions. Woodland and thick brush are likely impassable without a well-worn path wide enough for it, and even then under 10 mph (16 km).', NULL, NULL, 'Height 4 ft (1.2 m); width 5 ft (1.5 m); length 11 ft (3.4 m)', '970 lbs (437 kg)', 120, 1, NULL, 45000, '45,000 credits gasoline, 72,500 electric, 445,000 Solid Oxide, 890,000 nuclear. Weapons are extra.', 'Model NG-WM330 (Class: All-Terrain Motorcycle). A low, three-wheeled all-terrain trike from Chad Trantham, Matt Wontroba and H. Werkheiser (team leaders), two wheels at the front and one behind, with strong suspension, a reinforced frame and armour. Big and fitted with oversized wheels because it was meant for combat cyborgs, Headhunters and big D-Bees, it has also sold well to Vagabonds, nomads, explorers and adventurers wanting a tough one-rider bike for the wilds. Weapons hang on the front rack and the sides, and mercenary companies buy fleets of them for short patrols. Penalties: none on pavement, short grass, dirt roads and stony desert; -10% piloting on gravel and tall grass, -15% on broken roads, sand, and mud or snow up to 8 inches (20 cm); deeper mud and snow, forest and dense growth are likely impassable. It can cross sand dunes. Range: 400 miles (640 km) on gasoline; 2,000 miles (3,200 km) per charge on its standard multi-battery electric system; unlimited on Solid Oxide or nuclear. Cargo: a small compartment behind the back seat, about a small backpack or duffel bag, with room to strap on more. Weapons: none as standard; a light nose gun plus a weapon on each side, from the hovercycle options, may be added, and about half of buyers fit at least one.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.205-206');

